1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:01,720
Let's go, shall we!

2
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:03,480
Next up, Kame this way!

3
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:04,760
Nyahaha!

4
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:16,900
Anyone broke, come to me!

5
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:21,600
I'm broke too, but don't worry.

6
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:25,460
Look at that blue sky,

7
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:28,800
white clouds.

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,360
Something'll work out eventually.

9
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:38,640
You get it, right?

10
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:40,620
Got it, got it.

11
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:44,520
Once you understand,
just shut up and follow me.

12
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:18,860
Hey! Thief!

13
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:20,280
Take care!

14
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:21,640
Take care!

15
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:26,800
It's Kankichi!

16
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:30,740
Hey! What on earth is going on?

17
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:32,780
Pulling a stunt like a common thief!

18
00:01:33,260 --> 00:01:36,280
I didn't think you'd repay my kindness with treachery,
Kankichi!

19
00:01:36,460 --> 00:01:38,940
W-well, there's a good reason for this!

20
00:01:39,180 --> 00:01:40,060
A good reason?

21
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:44,140
Have you heard of the TV
show Tetsujin Baka Ichidai?

22
00:01:44,684 --> 00:01:49,400
the one where muscular guys show off their
strength and compete to their limits, right?

23
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:51,580
I watch it all the time with Grandma.

24
00:01:51,580 --> 00:01:54,340
I applied for it, and I got selected.

25
00:01:54,820 --> 00:01:55,980
That's amazing.

26
00:01:55,980 --> 00:01:58,740
Kankichi could maybe win it, you know.

27
00:01:58,740 --> 00:02:01,720
Right? The show's live tomorrow.

28
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:06,100
But I'm flat broke,
so I haven't eaten a thing since yesterday.

29
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:08,000
I've got no strength at all.

30
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,900
I asked the chief and the others,
but nobody would lend me money for a meal.

31
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:13,060
So I had no choice, and

32
00:02:14,220 --> 00:02:15,460
Even so,

33
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:17,420
I'm really sorry.

34
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:20,660
But if I win tomorrow's show,

35
00:02:20,660 --> 00:02:23,000
I'll be invited on a family trip to Hawaii.

36
00:02:23,440 --> 00:02:26,320
If you feed me sushi, I'll definitely win,

37
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:29,780
and I'll take everyone
at Riboshike to Hawaii.

38
00:02:29,780 --> 00:02:33,060
Knowing you, you'll say
"take us along" and then

39
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:35,120
charge us later, won't you?

40
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:37,160
I wouldn't do that.

41
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:40,200
Everyone here has always looked after me.

42
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:44,100
All we want is for them
to welcome us in Hawaii.

43
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:45,680
But I'd love to go to Hawaii!

44
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:47,680
Mom and I both want to go, don't we?

45
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:49,740
Well, if we could go for free, sure.

46
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:51,700
Don't let anyone get fooled.

47
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:53,480
This guy's a Ryotsu type, you know.

48
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:55,800
There's bound to be something behind this.

49
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:58,660
Come on, just this once, trust me!

50
00:02:58,660 --> 00:03:02,260
After the way you behave every day,
how could anyone trust you?

51
00:03:03,180 --> 00:03:04,880
Yeah, if we're going anyway,
let's head to Hawaii...

52
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:07,380
Why don't you open a
branch of Chōkanda Sushi?

53
00:03:08,140 --> 00:03:09,760
A branch in Hawaii

54
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:12,440
Yeah, I'm sure this sushi would be a hit.

55
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:15,980
I see. You really can
win the top prize, right?

56
00:03:15,980 --> 00:03:19,160
Yeah, it's a cinch as
long as I'm not hungry.

57
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:21,840
Alright, got it. Thanks.

58
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:23,100
Yes.

59
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:25,540
Feed him sushi till he's stuffed.

60
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:27,640
Understood, Mom.

61
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:29,480
Yay, I did it!

62
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:33,300
Thanks for the food.

63
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:41,540
You really pack it away, don't you?

64
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:44,160
You must've been really hungry.

65
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:48,160
No, I've eaten plenty of sushi here,
but it's still so good!

66
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,080
Be sure to win!

67
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:52,200
Leave it to me.

68
00:03:58,820 --> 00:04:01,640
And the final battle
is this push-up contest!

69
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:03,800
Things are getting out of hand.

70
00:04:04,260 --> 00:04:06,780
Both of them are about to pass 2,000 reps!

71
00:04:06,780 --> 00:04:09,360
Whoever wins, it's an incredible record.

72
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:10,980
Don't you dare lose!

73
00:04:10,980 --> 00:04:13,600
Just a little more!
The opponent's completely worn out!

74
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:15,140
Come on, Kankichi!

75
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:19,040
Whoa, Tanaka's finally down!

76
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:23,300
The count is 2,009,
and the winner is Kankichi Ryotsu!

77
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:24,600
Yay!

78
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:26,280
That's impressive.

79
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:29,780
He's an idiot, but he's got stamina,
I'll give him that.

80
00:04:29,780 --> 00:04:31,460
It's thanks to our sushi, isn't it?

81
00:04:31,460 --> 00:04:34,300
A new Iron Idiot has been born!

82
00:04:34,760 --> 00:04:36,880
His name is Kankichi Ryotsu.

83
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:38,780
He's won the Hawaii trip!

84
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:42,400
Check it out!
We're going to Hawaii for New Year's!

85
00:04:43,480 --> 00:04:47,740
The Gibōshike Party in Hawaiian Big Panic!

86
00:04:54,260 --> 00:04:55,380
What a crowd!

87
00:04:55,380 --> 00:05:01,300
They call it cake, but there sure are a lot of
rich folks planning to spend New Year's abroad.

88
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:06,620
Isn't that the producer and
staff of Tetsujin Baka Ichidai?

89
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:10,220
Hey! What are you guys
doing in a place like this?

90
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:12,740
Ryo-san, what are you saying?

91
00:05:12,740 --> 00:05:17,780
Of course, we're going to Hawaii with
all the past champions and their families!

92
00:05:18,140 --> 00:05:18,500
What?

93
00:05:18,780 --> 00:05:19,260
See?

94
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:27,080
W-what?
Wasn't the Hawaii trip just for my family?

95
00:05:27,440 --> 00:05:28,320
Come on.

96
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:35,260
I told you there's a Tetsujin Baka Ichidai TV taping in Hawaii,
a family competition among past champions, didn't I?

97
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:38,860
I never heard anything about that!

98
00:05:39,340 --> 00:05:41,720
It was mentioned at the start of the show.

99
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:43,700
Weren't you listening properly?

100
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:45,520
So that's how it was.

101
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:49,000
Anyway, please do your best
and work together as a family.

102
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:50,920
Well, this is a problem.

103
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:52,760
Having already said it was free,

104
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:54,320
I can't tell everyone.

105
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:56,520
If I did tell them...

106
00:05:57,540 --> 00:05:59,160
See? I told you.

107
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:01,580
There was a catch after all, wasn't there?

108
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:05,280
Going so far as to set up
a New Year's Hawaii package,

109
00:06:06,620 --> 00:06:08,800
So you made us race each
other at push-ups like that?!

110
00:06:09,140 --> 00:06:10,500
You idiot!

111
00:06:16,940 --> 00:06:19,060
It's probably going to turn out like that.

112
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:21,180
We've got to make this work no matter what.

113
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:23,100
without letting the old ladies find out.

114
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:25,600
I have to enter the race by myself.

115
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:27,700
Hey! Tankichi!

116
00:06:27,940 --> 00:06:28,780
What are you doing?

117
00:06:29,140 --> 00:06:31,600
Sorry, sorry! I'm coming right away.

118
00:06:33,780 --> 00:06:35,720
A family trip overseas, no less!

119
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:37,740
Yeah.

120
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:40,660
But you can take off your seatbelt now,
you know.

121
00:06:41,340 --> 00:06:42,160
Sorry about that.

122
00:06:42,820 --> 00:06:45,700
Kankichi, is it really all free?

123
00:06:45,700 --> 00:06:49,060
Of course!
The in-flight meal is coming up next.

124
00:06:49,060 --> 00:06:55,020
For the main course, they'll ask if you want chicken or beef,
so just order whichever you like.

125
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:57,140
I'd rather have the fish.

126
00:06:57,140 --> 00:07:01,880
Don't be so picky! Honestly, first-timers
on overseas trips are always like this.

127
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:07,000
Everyone, now I'll announce the
schedule once we arrive in Hawaii.

128
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:08,320
Uh-oh.

129
00:07:08,320 --> 00:07:10,740
Okay, okay, everyone look over here!

130
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:12,620
What is it, Kankichi?

131
00:07:12,620 --> 00:07:15,100
Since none of us have traveled abroad much,

132
00:07:15,100 --> 00:07:18,100
I'll explain the
life-saving equipment for you.

133
00:07:19,340 --> 00:07:22,560
The stewardess already explained that a little while ago,
didn't she?

134
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:27,040
Well, if something happens, it could be a matter
of life and death, so better safe than sorry.

135
00:07:27,040 --> 00:07:31,280
Okay, I'm explaining right now,
so could you please be quiet?

136
00:07:31,880 --> 00:07:33,220
It's getting worse and worse.

137
00:07:33,220 --> 00:07:33,900
That's right.

138
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:39,560
So we can listen to music?

139
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:41,200
Hey, aren't you ignoring us?

140
00:07:41,200 --> 00:07:43,040
Yay, Hawaiian dancers!

141
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:43,760
How lovely.

142
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:45,340
Nice.

143
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:50,080
Somehow I got away with it.

144
00:07:56,760 --> 00:07:57,800
How lovely.

145
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:59,440
You can see the ocean!

146
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:02,320
The wife and husband get this room.

147
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:03,320
Yes, meeting.

148
00:08:03,320 --> 00:08:04,640
Sorry about that.

149
00:08:05,460 --> 00:08:06,780
Sorry to keep you waiting.

150
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:16,740
Grandma and Lemon get Room 703 next door.

151
00:08:16,740 --> 00:08:17,520
Hey.

152
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:19,660
Hey, what about me?

153
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:25,360
That leaves me in this Room 704,

154
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:27,960
which means I'm stuck with Mato and me.

155
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:39,280
Wow, what an amazing view!

156
00:08:39,800 --> 00:08:42,640
Damn it,
I have to share a room with the old ladies?

157
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:44,320
Don't you think I hate it too?

158
00:08:44,780 --> 00:08:47,640
I've got some business to take care of,
so let's work out the plan.

159
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:48,980
I'm coming over now.

160
00:08:50,060 --> 00:08:52,460
I rented three cell phones.

161
00:08:52,460 --> 00:08:54,880
If anything happens, contact me.

162
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:55,820
Got it.

163
00:08:57,480 --> 00:08:58,120
Later.

164
00:08:58,680 --> 00:08:59,940
Bye-bye, Kankichi.

165
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:04,760
I'll be back before dinner, got it?

166
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:10,000
Alright, now the hard part begins.

167
00:09:14,340 --> 00:09:16,920
Everyone, please pay attention.

168
00:09:20,340 --> 00:09:24,420
First-leg runners, you'll start by bicycle.

169
00:09:25,340 --> 00:09:27,080
Family members can't come.

170
00:09:27,080 --> 00:09:29,220
They're all feeling unwell.

171
00:09:29,220 --> 00:09:31,040
Then is it dangerous?

172
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:33,660
No, I'll handle it all
by myself for everyone.

173
00:09:33,660 --> 00:09:35,520
Are you okay?

174
00:09:35,660 --> 00:09:39,920
It's a grueling race, cycling and
swimming all the way around Oahu.

175
00:09:39,920 --> 00:09:41,080
I'm fine.

176
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:44,120
Never mind that.
What do you actually get if you win?

177
00:09:44,420 --> 00:09:45,775
Well then, everyone,

178
00:09:45,825 --> 00:09:49,340
good luck aiming for the
100-million-yen grand prize.

179
00:09:49,340 --> 00:09:51,940
What? 100 million yen?

180
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:53,005
And also,

181
00:09:53,055 --> 00:09:57,640
families placing in the top three
will receive super luxurious prizes.

182
00:09:59,060 --> 00:10:00,880
Is that true?

183
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:02,520
Yes, of course.

184
00:10:02,520 --> 00:10:03,720
100 million yen

185
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:07,100
Alright, I'm definitely going to win this.

186
00:10:09,740 --> 00:10:13,620
Now, one Tetsujin Bakudan,
the start in Hawaii!

187
00:10:16,700 --> 00:10:18,260
The 30th champion,

188
00:10:18,310 --> 00:10:20,800
racer number 30, Kankichi Ryotsu,

189
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:22,780
has already taken a step ahead of the pack.

190
00:10:24,920 --> 00:10:26,400
Haina, is something wrong?

191
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:28,000
It's Kankichi?

192
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:31,100
I can't figure out how
to use this shake tea box.

193
00:10:32,140 --> 00:10:34,040
I can't put the cash away.

194
00:10:34,040 --> 00:10:36,040
Got it, I'm coming right now.

195
00:10:36,040 --> 00:10:36,940
Let's go.

196
00:10:36,940 --> 00:10:39,380
You're on the wrong course.

197
00:10:39,920 --> 00:10:40,620
Oops.

198
00:10:40,620 --> 00:10:44,360
The leader, racer number 30 Ryotsu,
has somehow left the course.

199
00:10:48,680 --> 00:10:50,940
It's written right here, you know.

200
00:10:50,940 --> 00:10:53,040
I don't really get it.

201
00:10:53,040 --> 00:10:55,120
Geez, what a pain.

202
00:10:55,120 --> 00:10:57,460
You enter a four-digit PIN code.

203
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,580
Even so, no,
I can't just take your word for it.

204
00:11:01,080 --> 00:11:10,600
Use a phone number or birthday, right? Like the home or shop number,
the eight-digit one, the 8810 from before.

205
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:16,360
There, that's set. Wow, you're amazing. When you want to open it,
press the number you just set.

206
00:11:16,360 --> 00:11:17,000
Got it.

207
00:11:19,460 --> 00:11:22,180
Going through the hotel?
What a huge waste of time.

208
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:26,500
And now, from here, is today's second race,
the long-distance swim.

209
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,440
Here the baton passes to the
second leg's runner, Kazuku.

210
00:11:29,440 --> 00:11:33,560
The racers have come all the
way back from Oahu by bicycle.

211
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:35,140
Everyone is exhausted.

212
00:11:35,140 --> 00:11:38,380
He was in the lead but
had strayed off course.

213
00:11:38,380 --> 00:11:40,460
Racer Ryotsu has returned.

214
00:11:41,520 --> 00:11:43,920
He's rejoined the race,
but now he's in the second leg.

215
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:45,920
Damn! Last place?! Alright,

216
00:11:45,970 --> 00:11:48,020
now I'm making a big comeback!

217
00:11:48,260 --> 00:11:48,520
Go!

218
00:11:55,060 --> 00:11:58,820
Huff, huff, huff, it's me!

219
00:11:59,380 --> 00:12:00,269
Kankichi,

220
00:12:00,319 --> 00:12:03,540
the TV switched to pay-per-view,
and I want to switch it back.

221
00:12:03,540 --> 00:12:05,260
Got it, I'm coming right away.

222
00:12:05,860 --> 00:12:08,400
Damn it, and I'd just caught up!

223
00:12:13,980 --> 00:12:16,566
Pay mode means it's a paid movie, you know.

224
00:12:16,616 --> 00:12:18,960
Do this and it goes back
to a regular channel.

225
00:12:19,340 --> 00:12:20,860
Can't you see this?

226
00:12:20,860 --> 00:12:22,380
It's a period drama!

227
00:12:24,880 --> 00:12:29,460
Thanks, but I've only ever stayed at inns,
so I have no idea about hotels.

228
00:12:29,460 --> 00:12:32,540
Read the instructions,
they're written in Japanese too.

229
00:12:33,620 --> 00:12:36,800
Twenty minutes wasted! Serves you right!

230
00:12:43,480 --> 00:12:46,960
Kankichi, the period drama
in Hawaii is in Japanese too

231
00:12:48,540 --> 00:12:50,440
Where did Kankichi go?

232
00:12:53,640 --> 00:12:55,280
A hundred million yen is riding on this.

233
00:12:55,280 --> 00:12:56,700
Late, Taribadas!

234
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:13,520
And in the lead is Ryotsu!

235
00:13:13,520 --> 00:13:16,080
Ryotsu passes in first place!

236
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:18,700
We've now entered the third race,
the marathon!

237
00:13:18,700 --> 00:13:20,620
Running solo in the lead
without a single change!

238
00:13:20,620 --> 00:13:22,100
What stamina!

239
00:13:25,620 --> 00:13:27,380
Not again. What is it?

240
00:13:27,380 --> 00:13:28,840
Citrus, is it?

241
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:31,120
I found a good shop, so I'm deciding on it.

242
00:13:31,120 --> 00:13:32,500
Hold on a second.

243
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:34,520
Isn't that a bit too fast, even so?

244
00:13:34,520 --> 00:13:37,040
Well, it's a pretty good property, you see.

245
00:13:37,040 --> 00:13:40,100
Anyway, Granny,
you can't even speak English, can you?

246
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:42,560
Well, that goes for you too, doesn't it?

247
00:13:43,200 --> 00:13:45,020
Anyway, don't sign the contract yet!

248
00:13:45,020 --> 00:13:48,000
I'm coming over now,
so tell me where you are.

249
00:13:50,680 --> 00:13:51,700
Alright, got it.

250
00:13:58,200 --> 00:14:02,080
The leader, Kankichi Ryotsu,
has gone down here!

251
00:14:03,060 --> 00:14:04,860
Even he is finding it tough.

252
00:14:05,400 --> 00:14:09,300
Ryotsu is the only one of the 30 teams competing alone,
without a family.

253
00:14:09,300 --> 00:14:13,360
He has kept going alone through cycling,
swimming, and running up to this point,

254
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:15,460
but now he has finally
reached his physical limit.

255
00:14:16,780 --> 00:14:17,920
Right, charging complete!

256
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:22,020
What a man! He recovered in just 20 seconds.

257
00:14:24,520 --> 00:14:26,080
What's going on with Ryotsu?

258
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:27,520
He suddenly started running the wrong way.

259
00:14:29,080 --> 00:14:31,620
But how am I supposed to manage in English?

260
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:35,960
Right, there should be a Nakagawa
Group company in Hawaii, too.

261
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:38,120
I'll ask one of their employees for help.

262
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:41,380
This contract is really alright, isn't it?

263
00:14:42,260 --> 00:14:44,040
Yes, it's a very good property.

264
00:14:44,040 --> 00:14:45,660
You found a good one.

265
00:14:45,660 --> 00:14:46,280
I see.

266
00:14:46,640 --> 00:14:50,560
Granny, we can just leave the rest to
this person from Nakagawa Real Estate.

267
00:14:50,560 --> 00:14:52,860
Is that so? Sorry for going out of your way.

268
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:56,020
Well then, I'm off.

269
00:14:58,680 --> 00:15:01,420
You came all the way to Hawaii
and you're still restless.

270
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:05,780
Well, the evening has nicely
settled in here in Honolulu.

271
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:09,080
This race began here
this morning on bicycles.

272
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:14,080
Passed down from swimming to the marathon and on through the family,
it has now returned here once again.

273
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:18,440
Crossing the finish line
first on day one is Team Suzuki.

274
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:19,340
Congratulations!

275
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:35,300
I made it through the first day's race,
and then some.

276
00:15:39,060 --> 00:15:43,800
Marathon, 75 points.
Swimming, first place with 100 points.

277
00:15:43,800 --> 00:15:48,220
Cycling was last with 0 points,
so we're in fifth place

278
00:15:49,120 --> 00:15:53,120
At this rate, will I last all three days?

279
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:55,820
This is fun.

280
00:15:59,440 --> 00:16:02,360
Wow, this is delicious.

281
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:04,640
Meat dishes are nice once in a while.

282
00:16:05,460 --> 00:16:08,140
Kankichi, what's wrong?

283
00:16:08,140 --> 00:16:11,700
You love steak, don't you?
You don't have any appetite!

284
00:16:11,700 --> 00:16:13,660
No, I'm fine.

285
00:16:15,040 --> 00:16:17,620
If the competition keeps going for three days like this,
I'll die.

286
00:16:17,620 --> 00:16:19,580
Starting tomorrow, I'll add some options.

287
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:21,700
I need to build up my stamina.

288
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:24,200
Alright, I'm going to eat!

289
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:28,660
Wow, Kankichi, you're something else.

290
00:16:28,660 --> 00:16:30,540
You don't have to eat like that.

291
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:39,180
Shopping, a relaxing cruise,
the one-day Hanauma Bay tour

292
00:16:39,940 --> 00:16:41,220
Are we going with this today?

293
00:16:41,220 --> 00:16:44,460
When in Hawaii,
we've got to enjoy the optional tours.

294
00:16:45,480 --> 00:16:49,080
It'll cost money,
but if we win, we'll manage.

295
00:16:49,640 --> 00:16:51,240
Sorry to keep you waiting.

296
00:16:51,700 --> 00:16:54,060
Look, the tour guide has come to pick us up.

297
00:16:54,060 --> 00:16:55,500
Look after everyone.

298
00:16:55,500 --> 00:16:59,040
Alright, everyone,
please head over to the bus.

299
00:17:01,980 --> 00:17:03,560
Kankichi, you're not coming?

300
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:07,180
I've got some errands to run today too.

301
00:17:07,180 --> 00:17:09,100
That's too bad.

302
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:11,480
Have fun!

303
00:17:15,820 --> 00:17:18,140
With this,
he shouldn't get called away again today.

304
00:17:18,140 --> 00:17:20,540
I should've added the option from the start.

305
00:17:21,700 --> 00:17:23,520
Tetsujin Baka Ichidai in Hawaii

306
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:25,260
The first event on day two

307
00:17:25,260 --> 00:17:27,260
is skydiving.

308
00:17:28,100 --> 00:17:30,200
You dive from an altitude of 1,000 meters

309
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:33,840
and see how close you can land
to the target on the ground.

310
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:36,340
The center is worth 100 points.

311
00:17:38,920 --> 00:17:40,200
Scary again.

312
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:44,020
Please jump in order,
starting with yesterday's top-ranked family.

313
00:17:45,220 --> 00:17:46,620
So we start fifth?

314
00:17:46,620 --> 00:17:48,640
But I'm good at diving.

315
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:50,500
I'll make up for yesterday's delay!

316
00:17:51,700 --> 00:17:53,920
Then, everyone, go for it with full energy!

317
00:17:56,340 --> 00:17:57,320
Aaaaaaah!

318
00:18:00,960 --> 00:18:03,020
I'm in such a good mood!

319
00:18:09,580 --> 00:18:18,620
Bathing my back in the moon's energy, transformed without any curry,
if it's a case in the sky with a Sailor stick lit in the dark, leave it to me!

320
00:18:19,280 --> 00:18:21,980
Moon-side master, Moonlight Detective!

321
00:18:22,700 --> 00:18:24,080
Just arrived!

322
00:18:24,080 --> 00:18:25,940
Venus Detective here too, nice to meet you.

323
00:18:25,940 --> 00:18:29,180
Hey! Why are you two showing up?

324
00:18:29,180 --> 00:18:34,380
The Special Investigations Division is currently on New Year's holiday,
on a trip to Hawaii.

325
00:18:34,380 --> 00:18:38,940
On top of that,
the TV station asked us to get in your way.

326
00:18:38,940 --> 00:18:43,780
What?! Just because you're a special,
don't force your way in!

327
00:18:44,340 --> 00:18:46,800
Moonlight Power!

328
00:18:51,140 --> 00:18:52,340
What's that supposed to be?

329
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:53,780
Allow me to explain.

330
00:18:53,780 --> 00:18:56,560
By transforming into Ogawa Roda,
Moonlight Detective

331
00:18:56,560 --> 00:18:59,840
can whip up a tremendously violent wind.

332
00:19:04,480 --> 00:19:05,980
Super intense!

333
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:08,240
What nonsense.

334
00:19:11,760 --> 00:19:13,160
Super intense!

335
00:19:14,040 --> 00:19:14,860
Yay!

336
00:19:17,420 --> 00:19:19,060
Now's the time to beat those guys!

337
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:24,700
What is it? You put me on the ceiling, sent me
out on the tour, and now you're calling me back?

338
00:19:24,700 --> 00:19:25,520
What's wrong?

339
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:26,280
What?

340
00:19:26,860 --> 00:19:29,180
I went shopping and got
shortchanged on my change.

341
00:19:29,180 --> 00:19:31,720
Fine, I'll come right away.

342
00:19:32,800 --> 00:19:33,780
Pretty big.

343
00:19:34,740 --> 00:19:37,740
Please, blow me off in that direction.

344
00:19:37,740 --> 00:19:38,260
What?

345
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:40,820
Telling me which direction?
How cheeky of you.

346
00:19:40,820 --> 00:19:43,600
Very well, I'll do as you wish.

347
00:19:44,860 --> 00:19:48,300
Roger! Out! Mares!

348
00:19:54,440 --> 00:19:57,260
So I told you the change was wrong,
didn't I?

349
00:19:59,960 --> 00:20:02,460
They don't understand Japanese at all.

350
00:20:03,760 --> 00:20:05,640
I wonder when Kankichi is going to get here.

351
00:20:05,640 --> 00:20:10,940
Sorry to keep you waiting.

352
00:20:11,580 --> 00:20:12,900
Kankichi.

353
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:19,360
Kaakichi.

354
00:20:19,360 --> 00:20:23,060
Don't you dare screw with Japanese tourists,
asshole!

355
00:20:23,060 --> 00:20:26,320
Sorry, here's your change back.

356
00:20:26,860 --> 00:20:29,300
So you can speak Japanese after all!

357
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:32,880
Well, see you.

358
00:20:33,980 --> 00:20:36,020
Same as always, you never bother, do you.

359
00:20:36,020 --> 00:20:37,900
Why do we have to use parachutes?

360
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:40,840
It's just like something
out of James Bond, 007.

361
00:20:41,280 --> 00:20:44,200
And now the contestants are crossing
the finish line one after another!

362
00:20:49,740 --> 00:20:51,000
Alright, good work.

363
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:54,840
But you landed way off the mark,
so you get zero points.

364
00:20:54,840 --> 00:20:55,780
Damn it!

365
00:20:57,120 --> 00:20:59,120
What's the next race, anyway?

366
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:04,780
Today's second race is a
longboard race around Oahu.

367
00:21:05,220 --> 00:21:07,240
Alright, surfing's my specialty!

368
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:08,460
I'll make up for it!

369
00:21:09,020 --> 00:21:10,400
Ready, set, go!

370
00:21:10,840 --> 00:21:12,240
Yeah!

371
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:15,460
Shut up!

372
00:21:20,040 --> 00:21:22,932
What's with

373
00:21:22,982 --> 00:21:26,660
those guys?

374
00:21:28,660 --> 00:21:32,220
Now, here's the first checkpoint:
the lifeguards!

375
00:21:32,940 --> 00:21:36,300
Rescue the drowning beauty and head for
the finish line on a two-person board!

376
00:21:37,200 --> 00:21:39,700
So basically,
all I have to do is save the girl, right!

377
00:21:44,520 --> 00:21:46,300
Okay, you grab on.

378
00:21:47,360 --> 00:21:48,420
Hey, shoot!

379
00:21:49,540 --> 00:21:51,160
Paddling while sitting is tough.

380
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:52,320
Since we're going by surfing,

381
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:54,860
once I catch a wave, you hold onto my back.

382
00:21:54,860 --> 00:21:56,260
Okay!

383
00:22:00,740 --> 00:22:01,980
Here it comes!

384
00:22:01,980 --> 00:22:03,160
One, two!

385
00:22:03,840 --> 00:22:05,020
Come on, grab on!

386
00:22:06,320 --> 00:22:07,380
Hey, shoot!

387
00:22:10,220 --> 00:22:12,440
Feels like I got a little bit of a bonus.

388
00:22:17,740 --> 00:22:19,120
How lovely.

389
00:22:20,020 --> 00:22:22,140
I wish I could have shown Kankichi too.

390
00:22:22,140 --> 00:22:28,060
Dear, thank you for all your
hard work over the years.

391
00:22:28,060 --> 00:22:31,720
I've put you through so much hardship all this time.
Thank you.

392
00:22:32,180 --> 00:22:35,560
No, thank you so much
for such a wonderful trip.

393
00:22:37,380 --> 00:22:39,580
From the company, as a token of its appreciation,
here's one more present.

394
00:22:39,580 --> 00:22:40,920
Oh my, what could it be?

395
00:22:40,920 --> 00:22:42,300
Go ahead and open it.

396
00:22:45,060 --> 00:22:48,260
Oh my, something this expensive!

397
00:22:48,260 --> 00:22:49,160
Let's see.

398
00:22:53,960 --> 00:22:55,740
It suits you very well.

399
00:22:55,740 --> 00:22:58,260
Dear, thank you so much.

400
00:23:03,860 --> 00:23:06,080
Hey, did you see that pendant just now?

401
00:23:07,380 --> 00:23:09,840
The tires on the Gelby were glittering.

402
00:23:10,360 --> 00:23:13,140
It's a treasure worth at least
a hundred thousand dollars.

403
00:23:13,140 --> 00:23:15,200
My heart's pounding again after so long.

404
00:23:21,100 --> 00:23:22,040
Hold on a second.

405
00:23:23,280 --> 00:23:24,080
Don't move.

406
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:26,680
Who do you think you are?

407
00:23:27,240 --> 00:23:29,920
Don't say a word,
or I'll put umbrella holes in your back.

408
00:23:30,840 --> 00:23:32,460
You're coming with us.

409
00:23:37,380 --> 00:23:38,720
It's the chairman!

410
00:23:44,740 --> 00:23:47,000
What the hell is this?

411
00:23:51,280 --> 00:23:53,420
What is that?

412
00:23:53,420 --> 00:23:54,220
Gaah!

413
00:23:54,480 --> 00:23:54,820
Whoa!

414
00:23:59,540 --> 00:24:01,800
Arira, arira, arira!

415
00:24:05,840 --> 00:24:08,060
Loving the sea, defending justice,

416
00:24:08,060 --> 00:24:09,780
who summoned me? Poseidon!

417
00:24:09,780 --> 00:24:12,060
Into the chest goes Tansu Nigon!

418
00:24:12,060 --> 00:24:15,160
Leave the sea incidents to us!

419
00:24:16,260 --> 00:24:16,960
What a chatterbox.

420
00:24:16,960 --> 00:24:19,100
Yasuruki Kat is my trademark -

421
00:24:19,100 --> 00:24:20,980
Dolphin!

422
00:24:20,980 --> 00:24:21,740
Dekagan!

423
00:24:23,420 --> 00:24:26,300
Windeger! Did you come to ruin the race too?

424
00:24:27,600 --> 00:24:30,280
Hahaha, I'm working a part-time
job over the New Year's holiday!

425
00:24:30,800 --> 00:24:31,980
Peep-peep!

426
00:24:32,480 --> 00:24:33,040
Whoa!

427
00:24:34,440 --> 00:24:35,360
Damn it!

428
00:24:37,960 --> 00:24:39,160
Not again!

429
00:24:39,760 --> 00:24:42,000
What is it? I'm kind of busy right now!

430
00:24:42,480 --> 00:24:43,180
Kankichi,

431
00:24:43,230 --> 00:24:46,980
It's terrible!
A robbery just happened on a cruiser!

432
00:24:47,180 --> 00:24:49,600
What? Got it! I'm on my way!

433
00:24:50,060 --> 00:24:52,020
Damn it! Get in!

434
00:24:58,280 --> 00:24:59,260
Dolphin Dagger!

435
00:24:59,600 --> 00:25:01,680
Sorry, but could you
watch this kid for a moment!

436
00:25:01,840 --> 00:25:02,480
Whoa!

437
00:25:03,180 --> 00:25:03,760
I'm counting on you!

438
00:25:04,860 --> 00:25:06,700
Hey! Wait a second, Ryotsu!

439
00:25:10,340 --> 00:25:10,900
Hey...

440
00:25:12,560 --> 00:25:13,560
Hmph...

